  "research_note": "THE SHERMAN HOUSE, built by T-3688 for the 1871 scene, from Carbutt's stereograph (No. 52) taken from a window across Clark Street: six storeys of Athens marble over a ground storey of arched shop fronts, three groups of windows on each front between pilaster strips, round heads in the end groups and flat heads under little cornices in the middle, a heavy bracketed cornice, an iron balcony over the shop fronts round both streets, a two-storey columned porch at the hotel's entrance on Clark Street and a balustraded attic over the south-east corner. The north and west walls (against neighbours) are built blank (docs/LIBERTIES.md, T-3688).",
